{{!-- The Faith Received rail.

     One navigation for the library, sitting between Mere Orthodoxy's
     masthead and the page. It replaces the per-page link rows that had
     grown up surface by surface: ten links in the all-works hero, a
     different six on the research page, and nothing at all on several
     others. Ian, 2026-09-21: "Remove all other navigation that isn't
     the Mere O navbar and replace it with this rail as the primary TFR
     nav function."

     WHERE IT GOES: landing pages, the tools, and (Ian, 2026-09-23) the
     reader, where it sits above the reader's toolbar and stays pinned
     with it when the masthead scrolls away. Not the TFR home, which has
     its own doors.

     SIX ITEMS, TWO OF WHICH OPEN. Read and Research carry
     more than one destination, so they are buttons that open a drawer
     along the rail rather than links that guess which destination you
     meant. Search and Topics go straight there, because there is only
     one place to go. The brand goes to the library's front door.

     The drawer is markup, not a fetch: every destination is known at
     build time, so the rail works before any script runs and the script
     only opens and closes things. --}}
{{!-- GATED, 2026-09-22 (Ian): "if someone clicks on one anywhere in
     TFR, they should get a small subscribe form pop-up that works
     properly". Each research link carries data-feature-gate, which
     assets/js/feature-gate.js intercepts in the capture phase for anyone
     without an account: the modal opens instead of the page, and the
     link still works the moment they have one. Reading links, Scripture,
     Topics and the Dictionary carry nothing and stay open.

     The tier these resolve to lives in ONE place, feature-gate.js's
     TFR_BETA_OPEN_TO_ALL_MEMBERS, checked against both library workers
     by website/workers/scripts/check-tfr-tier.mjs. --}}
<nav class="tfr-rail" aria-label="The Faith Received" data-keep-href>
  <div class="container tfr-rail-inner">

    {{!-- thefaithreceived.com 301s here, so this is the same door
         without the redirect hop or the trip off-origin. --}}
    <a class="tfr-rail-brand" href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received <span class="tfr-rail-home">| Home</span></a>

    <ul class="tfr-rail-items">
      <li><a class="tfr-rail-link" href="/the-faith-received/search/" data-feature-gate="tfr-search">Search</a></li>

      <li class="tfr-rail-group">
        <button type="button" class="tfr-rail-link tfr-rail-toggle" data-tfr-drawer="read" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tfrDrawerRead">Read</button>
        <div class="tfr-rail-drawer" id="tfrDrawerRead" data-tfr-drawer-for="read" hidden>
          <a href="/the-faith-received/curated/">Curated</a>
          <a href="/the-faith-received/all-works/?collection=all">Full Library</a>
          {{!-- The works that can be read beside the printed page
               (Ian, 2026-09-24). --}}
          <a href="/the-faith-received/scans/">Page Scans</a>
          {{!-- Every author in the library, by shelf (Ian, 2026-09-24). --}}
          <a href="/the-faith-received/authors/">Authors</a>
          {{!-- The library by church: an overview of each tradition with
               its creeds and confessions and its authors (2026-09-24). A
               way into the texts, so it sits in Read rather than taking a
               seventh place on the rail. --}}
          <a href="/the-faith-received/tradition/">Traditions</a>
          {{!-- The Dictionary is a book to read, not a workspace to
               work in, so it sits with the other two ways into the text
               rather than among the research tools. --}}
          <a href="/the-faith-received/dictionary/">Dictionary</a>
        </div>
      </li>

      {{!-- Scripture is one page now (Ian, 2026-09-22): the rebuilt reader
           replaced the Index and the ported Bible, so the drawer that
           chose between them is gone and the item goes straight there. --}}
      <li><a class="tfr-rail-link" href="/the-faith-received/scripture/">Scripture</a></li>

      <li><a class="tfr-rail-link" href="/the-faith-received/topics/">Topics</a></li>

      <li class="tfr-rail-group">
        <button type="button" class="tfr-rail-link tfr-rail-toggle" data-tfr-drawer="research" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tfrDrawerResearch">Research</button>
        <div class="tfr-rail-drawer tfr-rail-drawer--wide" id="tfrDrawerResearch" data-tfr-drawer-for="research" hidden>
          {{!-- Each goes to the page that owns it. Power Search,
               Bookmarks and Notebook have no standalone page, so they
               deep-link to the mode on the surface that carries them:
               both of those pages route on the hash. --}}
          <a href="/the-faith-received/ask/" data-feature-gate="ask">Ask</a>
          <a href="/the-faith-received/search/#power" data-feature-gate="tfr-search">Power Search</a>
          <a href="/the-faith-received/research/#compare" data-feature-gate="tfr-compare">Compare</a>
          {{!-- Called Connections, goes to Connections: Ian's instruction
               was to keep the name and change the destination. --}}
          <a href="/the-faith-received/connections/" data-feature-gate="tfr-connections">Connections</a>
          {{!-- Was /the-faith-received/pins/, which is the ported
               notebook and a different store from the Bookmarks panel on
               the Research desk. Ian, 2026-09-22: "Bookmark and Notebook
               in the navrail need to be the same thing as those on the
               research page." Both items now name the same two panels
               the Research desk shows; /pins/ forwards here as well. --}}
          <a href="/the-faith-received/research/#bookmarks" data-feature-gate="tfr-bookmarks">Bookmarks</a>
          <a href="/the-faith-received/research/#notebook" data-feature-gate="tfr-notebook">Notebook</a>
          <a href="/the-faith-received/desk/" data-feature-gate="tfr-desk">Desk</a>
        </div>
      </li>

      {{!-- The guided tours (Ian, 2026-09-25). Its home is the tutorial
           hub, /the-faith-received/tutorial/, which 404s until
           routes.yaml is uploaded; until then this starts the first tour,
           which chains to the rest. Point it at the hub once the route is
           live. --}}
      {{!-- About, a drawer rather than a link (Ian, 2026-09-25). The
           tutorial was the only way in here and the manifesto had none,
           so the two things a newcomer wants, what this is and how to
           use it, now sit together under one name. Same drawer as Read
           and Research; narrow, because it holds two items. --}}
      <li class="tfr-rail-group">
        <button type="button" class="tfr-rail-link tfr-rail-toggle" data-tfr-drawer="about" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tfrDrawerAbout">About</button>
        <div class="tfr-rail-drawer" id="tfrDrawerAbout" data-tfr-drawer-for="about" hidden>
          <a href="/the-faith-received/manifesto/">About TFR</a>
          <a href="/the-faith-received/tutorial/">Tutorial</a>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>
{{!-- The tour engine rides with the rail, so every page that has the rail
     can run a tour from ?tour=<name>. NOT deferred: it must read ?tour=
     before reader-core.js rewrites the reader's address, and the rail
     sits above reader-core.js in the reader template. It does nothing at
     load but read the address; its sheet loads only when a tour starts.
     See assets/js/page/faith-tour.js. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-tour.js"}}&amp;frv=24eb514a935c576c" data-css="{{asset "css/faith-tour.css"}}&amp;frv=79423a1f3bf7c440"></script>
